<title>USA: Image Sensing gets first large Asian order.</title>
<headline>Image Sensing gets first large Asian order.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Image Sensing Systems Inc, a maker of video-based traffic management systems, said Monday it received its first large order from an Asia-Pacific customer.</p>
<p>It said the $267,500 order came from its Korean distributor, KIA Information Systems Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Delivery is anticipated during the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>KIA was awarded the Olympic Road project in Seoul, South Korea.  The project will include 17 two-camera Autoscope systems along the freeway from Seoul to the airport.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
